{"unit":1,"items":54,"pass":38,"title":"Unit Test · Unit 1","tracks":{"a14":"Track_1.4.mp3","a15":"Track_1.5.mp3"},"SEGS":{"news":["a14",3.95,null],"voxpop":["a15",4.02,null]},"html":"\n  <section class=\"stage on\" data-stage=\"Unit Test\">\n    <div class=\"stage-head\">\n      <div class=\"kicker\">Unit 1 &middot; Unit Test</div>\n      <h2>Friends and money</h2>\n      <p>Six parts, <b>54 questions</b>, covering everything in Unit 1: vocabulary, grammar, reading, listening, functional language and one integrated part. Answer them all, then press Check. You need <b>38 out of 54</b> to pass. Parts 7 and 8 are your writing and speaking &mdash; they are not marked automatically, but do not skip them. You can take this test as many times as you like.</p>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"task\" data-task data-tid=\"review-u1\">\n\n      <!-- ============ PART 1 · VOCABULARY ============ -->\n      <div class=\"instruction\">Part 1 &middot; Vocabulary &nbsp;<span class=\"qcount\">questions 1&ndash;12</span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Choose the word that fits.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">1</span><span class=\"body\">We were at school together, so we have known each other for years and we still&hellip; about twice a month.\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"c\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">reunite</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">connect</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">meet up</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">2</span><span class=\"body\">She never tells anyone else what I say. I&hellip; her completely.\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"b\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">admit</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">trust</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">recognize</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">3</span><span class=\"body\">The coat was thirty per cent off. It was a real&hellip;\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"a\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">bargain</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">purchase</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">membership</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">4</span><span class=\"body\">The company publishes what it pays its workers, so people call the brand&hellip;\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"c\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">half-price</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">harmful</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">guilt-free</button></div></span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Match the beginning of each phrase to its ending. Click one on the left, then one on the right.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">5&ndash;9</span><span class=\"body\">\n        <div class=\"pairbox\">\n          <div class=\"pcol\">\n            <button class=\"pit\" data-side=\"l\" data-key=\"v1\">keep</button>\n            <button class=\"pit\" data-side=\"l\" data-key=\"v2\">fall out</button>\n            <button class=\"pit\" data-side=\"l\" data-key=\"v3\">get on well</button>\n            <button class=\"pit\" data-side=\"l\" data-key=\"v4\">buy something</button>\n            <button class=\"pit\" data-side=\"l\" data-key=\"v5\">have a lot</button>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"pcol\">\n            <button class=\"pit\" data-side=\"r\" data-key=\"v3\" data-short=\"with somebody\">with somebody</button>\n            <button class=\"pit\" data-side=\"r\" data-key=\"v5\" data-short=\"in common\">in common</button>\n            <button class=\"pit\" data-side=\"r\" data-key=\"v1\" data-short=\"in touch\">in touch</button>\n            <button class=\"pit\" data-side=\"r\" data-key=\"v4\" data-short=\"on credit\">on credit</button>\n            <button class=\"pit\" data-side=\"r\" data-key=\"v2\" data-short=\"over money\">over money</button>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Write the noun formed from the word in brackets.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">10</span><span class=\"body\">(<i>able</i>) Her greatest <input class=\"gap\" data-answer=\"ability\" data-why=\"<b>Able</b> &rarr; <b>ability</b>.\"> is listening to people.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">11</span><span class=\"body\">(<i>govern</i>) The <input class=\"gap\" data-answer=\"government\" data-why=\"<b>Govern</b> &rarr; <b>government</b>.\"> has announced a new rule about advertising.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">12</span><span class=\"body\">(<i>improve</i>) There has been a real <input class=\"gap\" data-answer=\"improvement\" data-why=\"<b>Improve</b> &rarr; <b>improvement</b>.\"> in the way the two of them talk to each other.</span></div>\n\n      <!-- ============ PART 2 · GRAMMAR ============ -->\n      <div class=\"instruction\" style=\"margin-top:26px\">Part 2 &middot; Grammar &nbsp;<span class=\"qcount\">questions 13&ndash;26</span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Choose the correct form.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">13</span><span class=\"body\">Be quiet for a second &mdash; I&hellip; to the news.\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"b\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">listen</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">am listening</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">have listened</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">14</span><span class=\"body\">We&hellip; each other since our first year at university.\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"c\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">know</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">are knowing</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">have known</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">15</span><span class=\"body\">This bag&hellip; to my sister &mdash; I only borrowed it.\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"a\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">belongs</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">is belonging</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">has belonged since</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">16</span><span class=\"body\">I&hellip; of changing jobs, but I have not decided anything yet.\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"b\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">think</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">am thinking</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">have thought</button></div></span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Put the verb in brackets into the correct form.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">17</span><span class=\"body\">(<i>not see</i>) I <input class=\"gap gap-lg\" data-answer=\"haven't seen|have not seen|haven&rsquo;t seen|havent seen\" data-why=\"From the past up to now &rarr; present perfect.\"> her since the wedding.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">18</span><span class=\"body\">(<i>change</i>) The way young people spend money <input class=\"gap gap-lg\" data-answer=\"is changing\" data-why=\"A change in progress around now &rarr; present continuous.\"> very fast at the moment.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">19</span><span class=\"body\">(<i>cost</i>) How much <input class=\"gap gap-lg\" data-answer=\"does it cost|does that cost\" data-why=\"<b>Cost</b> is a state verb &rarr; present simple, never <i>is costing</i>.\"> to join?</span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">20</span><span class=\"body\">(<i>meet up</i>) We <input class=\"gap gap-lg\" data-answer=\"meet up\" data-why=\"A regular habit &rarr; present simple.\"> after work from time to time.</span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Complete each sentence with the correct form.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">21</span><span class=\"body\">I <input class=\"gap gap-lg\" data-answer=\"don’t want|do not want\" data-why=\"<b>Want</b> is a state verb &rarr; <i>I don&rsquo;t want</i>, never <i>I am not wanting</i>.\"> another bag.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">22</span><span class=\"body\">We <input class=\"gap\" data-answer=\"have been\" data-why=\"With <b>since</b> you need the present perfect: <i>have been friends</i>.\"> friends since 2016.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">23</span><span class=\"body\">Sorry, but I <input class=\"gap gap-lg\" data-answer=\"don’t understand|do not understand\" data-why=\"<b>Understand</b> is a state verb &rarr; <i>don&rsquo;t understand</i>.\"> the question.</span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Write the second sentence so that it means the same as the first.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">24</span><span class=\"body\">I last spoke to him in March.<br>I <input class=\"gap gap-lg\" data-answer=\"haven't spoken to him since march|have not spoken to him since march|haven&rsquo;t spoken to him since march\" data-why=\"A starting point &rarr; <b>since</b> + present perfect.\"></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">25</span><span class=\"body\">The jacket is my brother&rsquo;s.<br>The jacket <input class=\"gap gap-lg\" data-answer=\"belongs to my brother\" data-why=\"<b>Belong to</b> + the owner. No continuous form.\"></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">26</span><span class=\"body\">She started her present job two years ago and she is still there.<br>She <input class=\"gap gap-lg\" data-answer=\"has worked there for two years|has had that job for two years|has been in that job for two years|has worked in that job for two years\" data-why=\"A period running up to now &rarr; present perfect + <b>for</b>.\"></span></div>\n\n      <!-- ============ PART 3 · READING ============ -->\n      <div class=\"instruction\" style=\"margin-top:26px\">Part 3 &middot; Reading &nbsp;<span class=\"qcount\">questions 27&ndash;34</span></div>\n      <p class=\"subline\">Read the whole text once before you answer anything.</p>\n\n      <article class=\"reading\">\n        <h3>The friend who lends you money</h3>\n        <p class=\"stand\">Money is the fastest way to find out what a friendship is actually made of.</p>\n        <p><span class=\"pmark\">A</span>Ask people what makes a good friendship and they talk about trust, communication and having a lot in common. Ask them what ended their last one and a surprising number say the same word: money. A study of two thousand adults in the United Kingdom found that around one in three had fallen out with a friend over a loan, and that most of the amounts involved were small &mdash; under a hundred pounds.</p>\n        <p><span class=\"pmark\">B</span>Dr Helen Ochieng, who has been studying the subject since 2015, is not surprised. &ldquo;A loan between friends has no paperwork and no date,&rdquo; she says. &ldquo;So the two people are free to remember it differently. One of them believes it was a gift. The other one is waiting.&rdquo; Neither of them says anything, because saying something feels rude &mdash; and the silence does the damage that the money never could.</p>\n        <p><span class=\"pmark\">C</span>Her advice is unromantic. If you lend money to a friend, agree a date out loud on the day you hand it over. If you are not willing to do that, she says, do not call it a loan at all. Give it, forget it, and keep the friendship instead. Most people find the first option far harder, which tells you something about how we talk to each other.</p>\n        <p><span class=\"pmark\">D</span>There is one more finding in the study, and it is the one people argue about. Friends who had lent each other money and been paid back on time reported <i>stronger</i> friendships afterwards than friends who had never lent anything at all. Something about the whole business &mdash; asking, agreeing, waiting, being repaid &mdash; appears to prove something that ordinary socializing never tests.</p>\n      </article>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Choose the best answer.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">27</span><span class=\"body\">The best title for this text would be\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"b\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">How to save money as a student</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">Why lending to a friend is a risk worth understanding</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">Why you should never trust anybody with money</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">28</span><span class=\"body\">According to paragraph A, the sums of money that ended friendships were\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"c\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">always more than a thousand pounds</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">never written down anywhere</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">usually quite small</button></div></span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">True, False, or Not given? Choose for each sentence.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">29</span><span class=\"body\">Dr Ochieng began her research in 2015. <select data-answer=\"T\" data-why=\"Paragraph B: she has been studying the subject <b>since 2015</b>.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option value=\"T\">True</option><option value=\"F\">False</option><option value=\"N\">Not given</option></select></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">30</span><span class=\"body\">The study was carried out in the United States. <select data-answer=\"F\" data-why=\"Paragraph A says two thousand adults <b>in the United Kingdom</b>.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option value=\"N\">Not given</option><option value=\"T\">True</option><option value=\"F\">False</option></select></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">31</span><span class=\"body\">Dr Ochieng has lent money to a friend herself. <select data-answer=\"N\" data-why=\"The text never says anything about her own loans.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option value=\"T\">True</option><option value=\"N\">Not given</option><option value=\"F\">False</option></select></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">32</span><span class=\"body\">Friends who were repaid on time said their friendship had got better. <select data-answer=\"T\" data-why=\"Paragraph D: they reported <b>stronger friendships</b> afterwards.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option value=\"F\">False</option><option value=\"T\">True</option><option value=\"N\">Not given</option></select></span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Answer the last two questions about the whole text.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">33</span><span class=\"body\">In paragraph B, what does Dr Ochieng think actually damages the friendship?\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"a\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">the fact that neither person says anything</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">the size of the loan</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">the paperwork</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">34</span><span class=\"body\">In paragraph C, <i>unromantic</i> is used to suggest that her advice is\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"c\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">unkind to the person who borrows</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">impossible for most people to follow</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">practical rather than sentimental</button></div></span></div>\n\n      <!-- ============ PART 4 · LISTENING ============ -->\n      <div class=\"instruction\" style=\"margin-top:26px\">Part 4 &middot; Listening &nbsp;<span class=\"qcount\">questions 35&ndash;40</span></div>\n      <p class=\"subline\">Read the questions first. Then play each recording twice.</p>\n\n      <div class=\"player\">\n        <button class=\"btn btn-audio\" onclick=\"playClip('news',this,'Stop')\">\n          <svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"currentColor\"><path d=\"M8 5v14l11-7z\"/></svg> Recording 1 &middot; the news report\n        </button>\n        <div class=\"wave\"></div>\n        <div class=\"meta\"><b>Navigate B1+ &middot; Audio 1.4</b>Original coursebook recording</div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"player\">\n        <button class=\"btn btn-audio\" onclick=\"playClip('voxpop',this,'Stop')\">\n          <svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"currentColor\"><path d=\"M8 5v14l11-7z\"/></svg> Recording 2 &middot; the shopping-centre interview\n        </button>\n        <div class=\"wave\"></div>\n        <div class=\"meta\"><b>Navigate B1+ &middot; Audio 1.5</b>Original coursebook recording</div>\n      </div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Recording 1. Complete the notes with one word or a number.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">35</span><span class=\"body\">Black Friday falls in the month of <input class=\"gap\" data-answer=\"november\" data-why=\"The report says the fourth Friday in <b>November</b>.\"> .</span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">36</span><span class=\"body\">The custom began in <input class=\"gap gap-lg\" data-answer=\"the usa|the united states|america|usa|the us\" data-why=\"The report says it started in <b>the USA</b>.\"> .</span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Recording 1. True or false?</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">37</span><span class=\"body\">The report mentions people being hurt in the crowds. <select data-answer=\"T\" data-why=\"It warns about injuries caused by people fighting over things.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option value=\"T\">True</option><option value=\"F\">False</option></select></span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Recording 2. Choose the best answer.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">38</span><span class=\"body\">What exactly does Lewis ask people to do?\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"b\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">shop only in small local shops all year</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">buy nothing at all for twenty-four hours</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">give what they save to charity</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">39</span><span class=\"body\">He says that a fifth of the world&rsquo;s population uses\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"c\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">about a fifth of its resources</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">about half of its resources</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">over eighty per cent of its resources</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">40</span><span class=\"body\">His reason for preferring local shops is mainly\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"a\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">environmental</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">financial</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">personal</button></div></span></div>\n\n      <!-- ============ PART 5 · FUNCTIONAL LANGUAGE ============ -->\n      <div class=\"instruction\" style=\"margin-top:26px\">Part 5 &middot; Functional language &nbsp;<span class=\"qcount\">questions 41&ndash;48</span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">What would you say? Choose the phrase that fits the situation.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">41</span><span class=\"body\">A colleague has just said something you think is wrong. You want to disagree without ending the conversation.\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"b\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">That&rsquo;s completely wrong.</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">I see what you mean, but&hellip;</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">I couldn&rsquo;t agree more.</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">42</span><span class=\"body\">You want to admit that the other person is partly right before you answer.\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"c\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">If you ask me&hellip;</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">I&rsquo;m not so sure.</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">That&rsquo;s a fair point.</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">43</span><span class=\"body\">You agree with your friend as strongly as it is possible to agree.\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"a\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">I couldn&rsquo;t agree more.</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">I suppose so.</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">It depends.</button></div></span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Where does each phrase belong? Click a phrase, then click a column.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">44&ndash;47</span><span class=\"body\">\n        <div class=\"sortbox\">\n          <div class=\"sortpool\"><button class=\"swd\" data-col=\"Post\">What do you reckon?</button><button class=\"swd\" data-col=\"Mail\">It seems to me that&hellip;</button><button class=\"swd\" data-col=\"Post\">If you ask me&hellip;</button><button class=\"swd\" data-col=\"Mail\">We would be grateful for your views.</button></div>\n          <div class=\"sortcols\"><div class=\"sortcol\" data-col=\"Post\"><h5>A post to friends</h5><div class=\"drop\"></div></div><div class=\"sortcol\" data-col=\"Mail\"><h5>An email to a company</h5><div class=\"drop\"></div></div></div>\n        </div>\n      </span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Put the three parts of the reply in the usual order.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">48</span><span class=\"body\">\n        <div class=\"order\" data-order=\"q2,q1,q3\">\n          <button class=\"ochip\" data-val=\"q1\"><span class=\"pin\"></span><span class=\"txt\">In my opinion, the price is the whole problem.</span></button>\n          <button class=\"ochip\" data-val=\"q2\"><span class=\"pin\"></span><span class=\"txt\">I see what you mean about repairs.</span></button>\n          <button class=\"ochip\" data-val=\"q3\"><span class=\"pin\"></span><span class=\"txt\">What do you reckon &mdash; would you pay double for one?</span></button>\n        </div>\n      </span></div>\n\n      <!-- ============ PART 6 · PUTTING IT TOGETHER ============ -->\n      <div class=\"instruction\" style=\"margin-top:26px\">Part 6 &middot; Putting it together &nbsp;<span class=\"qcount\">questions 49&ndash;54</span></div>\n      <p class=\"subline\">Complete the conversation. Every gap tests something from a different lesson in this unit.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"body\">\n        <div class=\"chat\">\n          <div class=\"msg\"><b>Dana</b>You look pleased with yourself.</div>\n          <div class=\"msg you\"><b>You</b>I <select data-answer=\"have just bought\" data-why=\"A finished action with a result you can see now &rarr; present perfect.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option>am just buying</option><option>have just bought</option><option>just buy</option></select> a jacket for half the price.</div>\n          <div class=\"msg\"><b>Dana</b>On credit?</div>\n          <div class=\"msg you\"><b>You</b>No. I <select data-answer=\"don&rsquo;t believe\" data-why=\"<b>Believe</b> is a state verb &rarr; present simple.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option>am not believing</option><option>haven&rsquo;t believed</option><option>don&rsquo;t believe</option></select> in paying for things later.</div>\n          <div class=\"msg\"><b>Dana</b>Sensible. Although the shops only cut prices to make you feel clever.</div>\n          <div class=\"msg you\"><b>You</b><select data-answer=\"That&rsquo;s a fair point,\" data-why=\"Admits the other side before you answer it.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option>You&rsquo;re completely wrong,</option><option>That&rsquo;s a fair point,</option><option>I couldn&rsquo;t agree more,</option></select> but I <select data-answer=\"have wanted\" data-why=\"A state that started in the past and continues &rarr; present perfect.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option>am wanting</option><option>have wanted</option><option>want since</option></select> this one since October.</div>\n          <div class=\"msg\"><b>Dana</b>Fine. Are you coming out on Friday?</div>\n          <div class=\"msg you\"><b>You</b>Can&rsquo;t &mdash; I <select data-answer=\"am meeting\" data-why=\"A fixed arrangement in the near future &rarr; present continuous.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option>meet</option><option>am meeting</option><option>have met</option></select> Aisulu. We <select data-answer=\"haven&rsquo;t seen\" data-why=\"From the past up to now, with <i>since</i> &rarr; present perfect.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option>don&rsquo;t see</option><option>aren&rsquo;t seeing</option><option>haven&rsquo;t seen</option></select> each other since we fell out in May.</div>\n        </div>\n      </span></div>\n\n      <button class=\"btn btn-primary\" onclick=\"checkReview(this)\" style=\"margin-top:24px\">Check my answers</button>\n      <div class=\"res\"></div>\n    </div>\n\n    <div id=\"reviewResult\" class=\"review-result\"></div>\n\n    <!-- ============ PART 7 · WRITING ============ -->\n    <div class=\"instruction\" style=\"margin-top:30px\">Part 7 &middot; Writing &nbsp;<span class=\"qcount\">assessed against the criteria</span></div>\n    <p class=\"subline\">Write 80&ndash;100 words. Give yourself fifteen minutes.</p>\n    <div class=\"opentask\" data-open data-tid=\"test-write\">\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"body\">\n        <p class=\"ohint\"><b>The task.</b> Somebody has posted this: <i>&ldquo;Nobody needs a new phone every two years. We are simply told when to want one.&rdquo;</i> Write a reply. Say whether you agree, give one reason, add one concrete detail from your own life, and finish with a question back to the writer.</p>\n        <textarea placeholder=\"I see what you mean, but&hellip;   In my opinion&hellip;   For example, my&hellip;   What do you reckon &mdash; ?\" data-track></textarea>\n      </span></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"bubble useful\">\n      <div class=\"blab\">Use at least four of these</div>\n      <ul>\n        <li>In my opinion&hellip; / It seems to me that&hellip; / If you ask me&hellip;</li>\n        <li>I see what you mean, but&hellip; / That&rsquo;s a fair point.</li>\n        <li>a state verb: <b>believe, think, mean, own, prefer, belong</b></li>\n        <li>a present perfect: <b>I have had mine since&hellip;</b></li>\n        <li>vocabulary from the unit: <b>on credit, bargain, guilt-free, resources, purchase</b></li>\n      </ul>\n    </div>\n\n    <!-- ============ PART 8 · SPEAKING ============ -->\n    <div class=\"instruction\" style=\"margin-top:26px\">Part 8 &middot; Speaking &nbsp;<span class=\"qcount\">assessed against the criteria</span></div>\n    <div class=\"opentask speak\" data-open data-tid=\"test-speak\">\n      <div class=\"sp-head\"><span class=\"sp-ic\">&#127908;</span>\n        <div><b>Speaking &mdash; ninety seconds, two parts</b><span>Extended turn</span></div></div>\n      <p class=\"sp-task\"><b>Part A.</b> Talk about one friendship: how long you have known each other, what you usually do, and one thing that is happening with it at the moment. <b>Part B.</b> Then answer this: <i>is it ever a good idea to lend money to a friend?</i> Give your opinion and one reason.</p>\n      <ul class=\"sp-list\">\n        <li>at least one present perfect with <i>for</i> or <i>since</i></li>\n        <li>at least one present continuous for something happening now</li>\n        <li>at least two state verbs in the simple form</li>\n        <li>one opinion phrase, and one phrase that softens a disagreement</li>\n      </ul>\n      <div class=\"sp-lang\"><b>Use this language</b>We&rsquo;ve known each other since&hellip; &middot; At the moment&hellip; &middot; I believe / I don&rsquo;t think&hellip; &middot; If you ask me&hellip; &middot; I see what you mean, but&hellip;</div>\n      <div class=\"rec\">\n        <div class=\"rec-row\">\n          <button class=\"rec-btn\" type=\"button\" onclick=\"recToggle(this)\" aria-label=\"Record your answer\" title=\"Record\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"currentColor\"><path d=\"M12 14a3 3 0 0 0 3-3V6a3 3 0 0 0-6 0v5a3 3 0 0 0 3 3zm5-3a5 5 0 0 1-10 0H5a7 7 0 0 0 6 6.9V21h2v-3.1A7 7 0 0 0 19 11z\"/></svg></button>\n          <div class=\"rec-label\"><b>Record your answer</b><span>Press the microphone and speak</span></div>\n          <div class=\"rec-wave\"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></div>\n          <div class=\"rec-time\">0:00</div>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"rec-takes\"></div>\n        <div class=\"rec-note\">Record it, play it back, then submit it for assessment.</div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"instruction\" style=\"margin-top:30px\">Parts 7 and 8 &middot; Assessment</div>\n    <p class=\"subline\">These two parts are not marked automatically and they are not marked by you. Submit your writing and record your speaking, then your teacher &mdash; or the AI tutor &mdash; scores each part against the criteria below and writes the feedback.</p>\n    <div class=\"rubric-slot\">\n      <ul class=\"reqlist\">\n        <li>my writing answers the whole task &mdash; opinion, reason, example, question back</li>\n        <li>it is between 80 and 100 words</li>\n        <li>I used at least two opinion phrases, and one of them softens a disagreement</li>\n        <li>I used at least four words from this unit</li>\n        <li>no state verb of mine is in the continuous form</li>\n        <li>I spoke for ninety seconds without stopping to translate</li>\n        <li>my spoken answer contained a present perfect with <i>for</i> or <i>since</i></li>\n        <li>I gave an opinion and a reason, not only an opinion</li>\n      </ul>\n    </div>\n  </section>\n"}